    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsSelfLink` test expected the owner response to include a `selfLink` field equal to `/api/owners/{id}`, but that field didn't exist. I added it in two places:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` response schema (which generates `OwnerDto.selfLink` at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", ...)` on `toOwnerDto` backed by a `selfLink(owner)` helper that returns `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` (null-safe when the owner hasn't been persisted).\n\nThis matches the codebase's existing pattern of expressing derived response fields as MapStruct expression mappings. The full test suite is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
